    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, led by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.85) and **Kyle Tucker** (75.65), both of whom benefit significantly from facing weak opposing starters. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a favorable matchup against Quantrill, while **Kyle Tucker** looks to exploit the vulnerability of V\u00e1squez. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Nasim Nunez** (71.50) also project as elite starts, buoyed by a substantial 16% park factor boost and a highly favorable matchup against Young. The combination of **Andy Pages** (71.21) and **Sam Antonacci** (61.12) further rounds out the offensive core, with **Sam Antonacci** seeing his value surge due to an optimal leadoff spot and strong xwOBA metrics.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup optimizer today was the exclusion of **Nolan Schanuel** (52.70), who missed the cut despite a respectable profile. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the higher projected efficiency of **Josh Lowe** (52.25) and **Jackson Merrill** (53.44) due to their platoon advantages and superior stolen base profiles\u2014a critical factor given our emphasis on speed. Managers should proceed with caution regarding the pending lineups for **Drake Baldwin**, **Josh Lowe**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Kyle Tucker**; while our projections assume their spots, any shifts in the batting order, particularly for **Josh Lowe** or **Drake Baldwin**, could trigger a downward adjustment in their efficiency scores. Furthermore, while **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** are confirmed starts, both face a stiff challenge against Griffin, whose elite-caliber ability to control the run game slightly suppresses their collective upside.",
